    "created_at": "2021-09-07T19:16:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-07T19:16:57Z",
    "body": "Per spec, downloads (just like 204s) will bail out of the navigate algorithm. This results in no navigation (not to about:blank) or load event, for successful downloads. It just spins up a separate algorithm to do the actual downloading.\r\n\r\nFor downloads blocked by sandboxing, the same thing occurs, just the algorithm bails out before doing the downloading.\r\n\r\nSo it looks like Chrome and Safari's behavior is the one that is correct per spec. And this also seems like it's probably by design; letting the sandboxed page know that you're preventing it from doing the bad thing seems unwise.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
